; Six camps ringed around the village rather than three on one side. Three camps meant that
; leaving by the only gate showed you one of them and the other two were behind the walls,
; which reads as an empty map however many creatures are actually standing in it.
;
; Distances are the minimum the audit allows for each roster: the hopper camps are nearest
; because a hopper gives up soonest, and the sprite camps are furthest because a sprite
; follows longest. Composition and respawn are data; these coordinates are the level design.

